Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Makes Chrome always print to the WINDOWS default printer instead of whichever
; printer it happened to use last.
;
; Without this, Chrome remembers the last printer per profile. Printing one
; thing to a real printer in an ordinary Chrome window then silently redirects
; the shipping labels to paper too -- with no preview to warn you, because
; silent printing is the whole point.
;
; With this set, Chrome ignores its own memory and follows Windows. Set
; PDFCreator as the Windows default and labels always go there.
;
; Double-click this file and approve the prompt. Restart Chrome afterwards.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Google\Chrome]
"PrintPreviewUseSystemDefaultPrinter"=dword:00000001
